{%- comment -%}
  ITM Group Card Image
  --------------------
  Resolves the photo shown on an itm-card-product-group "Shop Range" card.
  A hub collection like "Chrome Sockets" has no products of its own and no
  image of its own either — its real content is entirely its
  product_group_children (1" Drive Chrome Sockets, 1/2" Drive Chrome
  Sockets, etc.), and THOSE can themselves be hubs with no image, one level
  further down (e.g. 1" Drive Chrome Sockets has no image but points at
  Chrome Sockets - 1" Drive Metric, which finally has real products).
  Rather than show "image coming soon" the moment the first level comes up
  empty, this borrows a photo from the first child, recursing as many
  levels as it takes to reach a collection with a real image or a real
  product — same thing a person would do browsing the category tree by
  hand.

  Params:
    - collection (Collection) — required
    - depth (number) — internal recursion guard; never pass this in
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign depth = depth | default: 0
  assign found = false
-%}
{%- if collection.image -%}
  <div class="sbc__slide is-active">
    {{ collection.image | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: collection.title }}
  </div>
  {%- assign found = true -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Same primary-product resolution as the card itself: the
    primary_product_ref metafield NetSuite writes first, then the older
    per-product boolean flag, then just the first product.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign primary_product = collection.metafields.custom.primary_product_ref.value -%}
  {%- if primary_product == blank -%}
    {%- for p in collection.products -%}
      {%- if p.metafields.custom.primary_product -%}
        {%- assign prim_val = p.metafields.custom.primary_product.value | default: p.metafields.custom.primary_product -%}
        {%- if prim_val == true or prim_val == 'true' or prim_val == 1 or prim_val == '1' -%}
          {%- assign primary_product = p -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if primary_product == blank and collection.products.first -%}
    {%- assign primary_product = collection.products.first -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if primary_product -%}
    {%- assign group_sku = primary_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | default: primary_product.title | strip -%}
    <div class="sbc__slide is-active">
      <img
        src="{% render 'itm-cdn-product-image', sku: group_sku, image_number: 1 %}"
        data-cdn-fallback-src="{{ 'image_coming_soon.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt="{{ primary_product.title | escape }}"
        width="600"
        height="600"
        loading="lazy"
      >
    </div>
    {%- assign found = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- unless found -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Still nothing on this collection — borrow the first real child's photo
    instead, recursing further if that child is ALSO an empty hub. Capped
    at 5 levels as a sanity guard against a metafield loop; the real tree
    never goes past 6 levels total.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign kids = collection.metafields.custom.product_group_children.value -%}
  {%- if depth < 5 and kids != blank and kids.size > 0 -%}
    {%- assign next_depth = depth | plus: 1 -%}
    {% render 'itm-group-card-image', collection: kids.first, depth: next_depth %}
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="sbc__slide is-active">
      <img src="{{ 'image_coming_soon.png' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ collection.title | escape }}" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endunless -%}
